Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a “card” that flips (rotates) when you hover over it.  
It uses only HTML and CSS – no JavaScript.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Obracająca się karta</title>
<style>
/* 1️⃣  Set up the 3‑D environment */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  perspective: 800px;          /* Gives depth to the 3‑D effect */
  margin: 50px auto;           /* Center horizontally */
}

/* 2️⃣  The card itself – the element that will rotate */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d; /* Allows children to be positioned in 3‑D space */
  transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* Smooth animation */
}

/* 3️⃣  Flip the card on hover */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);   /* Rotate around the Y‑axis */
}

/* 4️⃣  Front & back faces */
.card-face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden; /* Hide the backside when it's turned away */
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

.card-front {
  background: #fff;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #333;
}

.card-back {
  background: #f8f8f8;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);   /* Position it behind the front */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: #555;
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-face card-front">
      Front side
    </div>
    <div class="card-face card-back">
      Back side
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| 1️⃣ | `perspective` on `.card-wrapper` | Creates a 3‑D space so rotations look realistic. |
| 2️⃣ | `transform-style: preserve-3d` on `.card` | Keeps child elements (`.card-face`) in 3‑D space. |
| 3️⃣ | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on hover | Rotates the whole card 180° around the Y‑axis. |
| 4️⃣ | `backface-visibility: hidden` on faces | Hides the face that is turned away from the viewer. |
| 4️⃣ | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on `.card-back` | Positions the back face behind the front so it becomes visible after rotation. |

Feel free to replace the text inside `.card-front` and `.card-back` with images, icons, or any content you like. Adjust the `width`, `height`, `perspective`, and `transition` values to fit your design.
